.TH WLPIPES 1 "2026-08-21" "wlpipes 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wlpipes \- the Windows 95 3D Pipes screensaver, for Wayland
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wlpipes
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wlpipes
grows coloured pipes through a three dimensional box, turning at right angles
and sprouting ball joints, until the box is full and the scene restarts.
.PP
By default it covers every connected monitor with a fullscreen
.B wlr-layer-shell
overlay, above panels and bars, and exits as soon as you press a key, click,
move the pointer or touch the screen. It is intended to be launched by an idle
daemon such as
.BR hypridle (1).
.PP
The compositor must support
.BR wlr-layer-shell-unstable-v1 .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Surface
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-windowed
Draw into an ordinary window instead of a fullscreen overlay. Use this while
developing: the compositor keeps ownership of the keyboard.
.TP
.B \-\-overlay
Fullscreen layer-shell overlay. The default.
.SS Scene
.TP
.BI \-\-grid " WxHxD"
Cells in the box. Default 26x20x26. Smaller grids give visually larger pipes.
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " MS"
Milliseconds per pipe segment. Default 60. Independent of the display's refresh
rate, so growth looks the same on a 60Hz and a 240Hz panel.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-runs " N"
Pipe runs drawn before the box is wiped and the scene restarts. Default 12.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-length " N"
Upper bound on a run's length. Default 100. Each run picks its own below this.
.TP
.B \-\-rotate
Slowly orbit the camera. Off by default; the original's camera was static.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Fixed random seed, to reproduce a particular scene.
.SS Lifecycle
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-seconds " N"
Exit after N seconds.
.IP
The overlay takes an exclusive keyboard grab, so a fault in its input handling
would leave the session untypeable. This is the escape hatch, and is worth
using whenever you are changing how input is handled.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Dismissed normally, or the deadline passed.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime failure, such as no compositor or no layer-shell support.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage: an unknown option, a missing value, or a value out of range.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the screensaver as an idle daemon would:
.PP
.RS
.B wlpipes
.RE
.PP
Watch it in a window while changing the simulation:
.PP
.RS
.B wlpipes \-\-windowed \-\-grid 12x10x12 \-\-speed 20
.RE
.PP
Reproduce one particular scene:
.PP
.RS
.B wlpipes \-\-seed 42 \-\-max\-seconds 30
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/wlpipes/hypridle.conf.example
An example idle daemon configuration.
.SH HYPRLAND
The overlay appears in
.B hyprctl layers
under the namespace
.BR wlpipes ,
on the overlay layer. Compositor rules can target it by that name, for example
to suppress the open animation:
.PP
.RS
.B layerrule = noanim, wlpipes
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hypridle (1),
.BR hyprlock (1)
.SH AUTHORS
The pipe growth algorithm follows xscreensaver's
.I hacks/glx/pipes.c
by Marcelo Vianna (1997), including its turn probability curve and colour
palette.
